class Solution {

    Node removeDuplicates(Node head) {

        if (head == null || head.next == null) return head; // Empty or single-node DLL.

        Node temp = head; // Start traversing from the head.

        while (temp != null && temp.next != null) { // Traverse while a next node exists.

            Node nextNode = temp.next; // Start checking from the next node.

            while (nextNode != null && nextNode.data == temp.data) { // Skip all duplicate nodes.
                nextNode = nextNode.next;
            }

            temp.next = nextNode; // Connect current node to the next distinct node.

            if (nextNode != null) {
                nextNode.prev = temp; // Update the previous pointer of the next distinct node.
            }

            temp = temp.next; // Move to the next distinct node.
        }

        return head; // Return the modified DLL.
    }
}
Time Complexity: O(n) – Every node is visited at most once while traversing the sorted doubly linked list and skipping duplicates.
Auxiliary Space: O(1) – Only a few pointer variables are used; no extra space proportional to the input size is required.
